[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2944909363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107151#issuecomment-2944909363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107151","id":2944909363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6vh8Az","user":{"login":"retrotails","id":10767978,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNzY3OTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10767978?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails","html_url":"https://github.com/retrotails","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/retrotails/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-05T15:02:35Z","updated_at":"2025-06-05T15:02:35Z","body":"> A deeper dive into _why_ this caused a regression in the first place is probably warranted at some point, but that's understandably outside the scope of this PR\r\n\r\nmy guess as to what's happening:\r\n\r\n`work_memory` is an array that holds light data for the voxels. it gets initialized filled with `1e20` as default values, which are supposed to all get overwritten with the actual light data, as it gets calculated. the very last step, after all the light contribution, converts those floats down into `uint8_t` (after taking the sqrt).\r\nwhen casting `sqrt(1e20)` (which is `1e10`) into `uint8_t`, c++ ends up with `1410065408` because the conversion overflows. which is probably a bug, but it happens to be a massive value (max is 255 and it gets clamped) so it works.\r\nwhen 1e20 was instead INFINITY; `sqrt(INFINITY) == INFINITY`. casting `INFINITY` to `uint8_t`, c++ chooses `0`, which I think is a special value in the voxel code. perhaps 0 is empty space and 1-255 are light values.\r\n\r\nas to why enabling shadows with spotlights specifically makes this crop up, I'm not sure. perhaps the voxel data ends up with some invalid values that only get read in certain circumstances, hence why baking crashes but only sometimes.\r\n\r\nthat's a lot of speculation though, I don't know much about the voxel GI stuff or C++ and it's not well documented in the code.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2944909363/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2944993895","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107151#issuecomment-2944993895","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107151","id":2944993895,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6viQpn","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://ap